hospital/a-79921240--e9705d91e6bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-s-last-ebola-patient-leaves-hospital/a-79921240?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kenya had nine confirmed cases, while DR Congo continues to battle its deadliest outbreak of the disease.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil electoral court fines Meta, sees no deliberate election bias</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7ddf4a7388c56fbb1bd8b5bef9bba4714e79249c95894f02a37d895164ef10b</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias/a-79920780--215a8f08f312.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias/a-79920780?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The fine came after President Lula's coalition filed a complaint. The court said there was no evidence of intent to influence the election. Meta said it will defend itself against "false allegations."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61f30b78f6f3bacf1fcd9b3ace29991d8fcf0e8d392ea5e49b7d99c57cd14560</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AIIB has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms and greater transparency are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcd0aa94aaf588142d67854cb394175367706cba515d5636114e82b364cdd8ae</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy: Hundreds of schools evacuated after bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:438280de9b236181b6e8401b26d2170cc922b600a0d8009dae239ec6e02d786d</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-hundreds-of-schools-evacuated-after-bomb-threats/a-79918034--3d07ea5d3a16.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-hundreds-of-schools-evacuated-after-bomb-threats/a-79918034?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Although the government believes the threat to be a hoax, it has nevertheless prompted concerns about "hybrid warfare" in Europe. Similar messages were sent in Northern Ireland, Ireland, and Bulgaria.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tundu Lissu: After escaping the death penalty, what does his guilty verdict mean for Tanzania's democracy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f4a4cee16e59547ce6f0927a40ca8c80c7f927577d65dd59894b1bcbbc465df</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T13:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tundu-lissu-after-escaping-the-death-penalty-what-does-his-guilty-verdict-mean-for-tanzania-s-democr/a-79908512--3044020567d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tundu-lissu-after-escaping-the-death-penalty-what-does-his-guilty-verdict-mean-for-tanzania-s-democracy/a-79908512?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A treason trial could have meant death by hanging for Tanzanian opposition leader Tundu Lissu. Instead, he now faces four years in prison for incitement to unrest. Can voices of dissident truly be heard in the country?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Only 1/3 of Germans satisfied with state of democracy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4bf2b655edb2a83799cca1fabc3f32c4eb56db764911c047fcb3c4409f99b39</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-only-1-3-of-germans-satisfied-with-state-of-democracy/live-79915066--348a315bae46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-only-1-3-of-germans-satisfied-with-state-of-democracy/live-79915066?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new authoritarianism study has revealed a new low in satisfaction levels with the functioning of German democracy. Meanwhile, the Bundeswehr has banned Chinese-made drones. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran classes Argentina navy, air force as 'terrorist organizations'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e4dc5d11a1eba15787f78a0b2e6f88955c7f999c2c0099f8211ac68cbfacf74</id><updated>2026-11-12T07:26:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-classes-argentina-navy-air-force-as-terrorist-organizations/a-79916290--7a72e35dd7c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-classes-argentina-navy-air-force-as-terrorist-organizations/a-79916290?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In a tit-for-tat move, Iran has said it now considers Argentina's navy and air force as "terrorist organizations." Tehran claimed Buenos Aires is responsible for further consequences.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
